# {{name}}

A Roblox game built on [StudWork](https://github.com/RandyjCrowley/studwork) {{tag}}, as a
single-game project: this repository is the game, and StudWork is the git submodule `studwork/`,
pinned at a release tag.

- Design doc: [docs/design.md](docs/design.md)
- Modules: {{modules}}
- Rules for agents and contributors: [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md)

## Set up (fresh clone)

```sh
git submodule update --init   # fetch studwork/ at the pinned tag
tools/install                 # toolchain (rokit) + Wally packages into studwork/deps/ + pre-commit hook
tools/doctor                  # checks the toolchain, packages, hook, framework pin, .env keys
```

## Everyday commands

```sh
tools/dev                     # rojo serve on port {{port}} + Studio connect steps
tools/format                  # stylua: fixes the formatting tools/lint checks (--check only checks)
tools/lint                    # selene + stylua --check + sync-projects --check + guardrails + framework pin
tools/typecheck               # luau-lsp strict (the first run downloads the Roblox type definitions into
                              # .cache/, git-ignored; `--offline` never downloads)
tools/test                    # Lune specs (Boot.spec boots the game in the multi-server sim;
                              # GameModule.spec shows how to spec the game module against the kits)
tools/build                   # rojo build -> build/{{name}}.rbxl
tools/make-module <Name>      # a new module in modules/<name>/, mapped in default.project.json
tools/make-screen <Name>      # a React screen in src/client/Screens/
tools/make-migration <module> # a save migration
tools/sync-projects           # regenerate kit module entries after changing GameConfig.modules
tools/net                     # Blink codegen after editing a .blink file
tools/framework-status        # the pinned StudWork tag vs the version stamped in deploy.json
```

The pre-commit hook runs `tools/lint` and `tools/test` before every commit. Writing specs:
`studwork/docs/framework/testing.md`.

## Publish

1. Create a test and a live experience on Roblox and an Open Cloud key with only
   `universe-places:write` for them; put it in the git-ignored `.env`
   (`cp .env.example .env`).
2. Put the universe/place ids in `deploy.json` (placeholders are 0; publish refuses them).
3. `tools/publish --test --dry-run`, then `tools/publish --test`, playtest, then
   `tools/publish --live` (refused unless the same build went to test first). Commit the stamped
   `deploy.json`.

Details: `studwork/docs/framework/publishing.md`.

## Bump StudWork

Read `studwork/CHANGELOG.md`, then:

```sh
git -C studwork fetch --tags && git -C studwork checkout vX.Y.Z
tools/install && tools/lint && tools/test
git commit -m "StudWork vX.Y.Z" studwork   # the bump goes in its own commit
```

Never edit files inside `studwork/`: `tools/lint` refuses local changes there and a submodule that
is not exactly at a release tag. Requests for the framework go in `FRAMEWORK_REQUESTS.md`.
